<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23418" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnhaeresco</span></b> , haesi, haesum,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i> [inhaereo], <i>to stick fast</i>, <i>cleave</i>, <i>adhere to.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in sordibus aurium, tamquam in visco,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 57, 144</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne quid emineret ubi ignis hostium
					inhaeresceret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					C. 2, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sucus villis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 17, 37, § 74</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poëtae inhaerescunt penitus in
					mentibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 3, 2, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
